<div id="S9.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">genus <math id="S9.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S9.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=60</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S9.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="62" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>62</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">62</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S9.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>69</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">69</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S9.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">genus <math id="S9.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S9.I2.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=95</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S9.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">genus <math id="S9.I2.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S9.I2.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=94" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>94</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=94</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S9.I2.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="119" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>119</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">119</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S9.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Again, it is straightforward to apply Corollary <a href="#Thmthm11" title="Corollary 11. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Primitive Algebraic Points on Curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> to these
curves. We computed all primitive points of certain low degrees on the genus
<math id="S9.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>
bielliptic curves <math id="S9.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}(60)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>60</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}(60)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}(62)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>62</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}(62)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For these two curves
the
size of the Mordell–Weil group has been computed by Najman and Vukorepa
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. We computed models for these curves
and Mordell–Weil generators using a <span id="S9.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Magma</span>
package developed by Ozman and Siksek
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, Adžaga, Keller, Michaud-Jacobs, Najman, Ozman and
Vukorepa <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, and Najman and Vukorepa <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>.
All computations were performed in <span id="S9.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Magma</span>. We summarize
our results in Table <a href="#S9.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 9. Low degree primitive points on some 
        
          
            ⁢
            
              
              X
              0
            
            
              
              
                (
                N
                ) ‣ Primitive Algebraic Points on Curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and
refer the reader to</p>
<table id="S9.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span id="S9.Ex23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/MaleehaKhawaja/Primitive" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/MaleehaKhawaja/Primitive</a></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.3" class="ltx_p">for the supporting code as well as a description of the points.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We also give a description of all
effective degree <math id="S9.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> divisors <math id="S9.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S9.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(D)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(D)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and
refer the reader to Table <a href="#S9.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 9. Low degree primitive points on some 
        
          
            ⁢
            
              
              X
              0
            
            
              
              
                (
                N
                ) ‣ Primitive Algebraic Points on Curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for this summary.</p>
</div>
