<td id="S9.T3.2.8.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S9.T3.m81" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3. </span>
For each pair <math id="S9.T3.m92" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,d)</annotation></semantics></math>, the table gives a description of the
effective degree <math id="S9.T3.m93" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> divisors <math id="S9.T3.m94" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S9.T3.m95" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(D)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(D)=1</annotation></semantics></math>
on the modular curve <math id="S9.T3.m96" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}(N)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We denote by <math id="S9.T3.m97" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{d,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{d,r}</annotation></semantics></math> the number of such divisors
that are reducible,
<math id="S9.T3.m98" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{d,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{d,p}</annotation></semantics></math> the number of such divisors
that are irreducible and primitive,
and
<math id="S9.T3.m99" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{d,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{d,i}</annotation></semantics></math> the number of such divisors
that are irreducible but imprimitive.
The symbol <math id="S9.T3.m100" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that we did not carry out the
computation for the pair <math id="S9.T3.m101" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,d)</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">10. </span>Data Availability Statement</h2>

<div id="S10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The data related to this paper is available at</p>
